Since $p$ and $q$ are inversely proportional, we have $p \times q = k$ for some constant $k$. Using the given values $p=25$ and $q=6$, we can find the constant $k$.
\begin{align*}
p \times q &= k\\
25 \times 6 &= k\\
k&=150
\end{align*}
Now, we want to find the value of $p$ when $q=15$. Using the equation $p \times q = k$, we have
\begin{align*}
p \times 15 &= 150\\
p &= \frac{150}{15}\\
p&=10
\end{align*}
Therefore, the answer is $p=10$.</think> <answer>10</answer>

